    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d229">

                <pb facs="0461" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E.W./9–1244</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Joint Chiefs of Staff
                        to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quebec</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-12">12 September 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: With reference to your
                    letter of 9 September regarding Norway,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d229-f1"/> it will
                    be noted from the enclosed copies of messages to General Deane that the Joint
                    Chiefs of Staff have instructed him as indicated in the third paragraph of your
                    letter.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Joint Chiefs of Staff:<lb/><signed>A J <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >McFarland</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Brigadier General,
                        U.S.A. Secretary</hi></closer>




